@startuml sequence_profile_view
' Sequenzdiagramm: Profil abrufen und anzeigen
' Zeigt den vollständigen Datenabruf mit Skills und Projekten

title Sequenzdiagramm - Profil anzeigen

actor Benutzer
participant "Browser\n(React)" as Browser
participant "Redux Store\n(RTK Query)" as Redux
participant "profileApi" as API
participant "ProfileController" as Controller
participant "ProfileServiceImpl" as Service
participant "ProfileRepository" as Repository
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

== Seitenaufruf ==
Benutzer -> Browser: Navigation zu /profile/me
Browser -> Redux: useGetProfileQuery('me')
Redux -> Redux: Prüfe Cache
alt Daten im Cache
  Redux --> Browser: Cached Profile Data
else Keine Daten im Cache
  Redux -> API: fetch('/v1/profiles/me', {Bearer Token})
  API -> Controller: GET /v1/profiles/{userId}
  
  == Autorisierung ==
  Controller -> Controller: authorizationUtils.resolveUserId('me', principal)
  note right: Extrahiert User-ID aus JWT\n(principal.getName())
  
  Controller -> Service: profileService.getProfile(userId)
  
  == Datenabruf ==
  Service -> Repository: findProfileByUserId(userId)
  Repository -> DB: SELECT ep.*, u.*, p.position_name, l.location_name\nFROM employee_profiles ep\nJOIN users u ON ep.user_id = u.id\nLEFT JOIN positions p ON ep.position_id = p.id\nLEFT JOIN locations l ON ep.location_id = l.id\nWHERE ep.user_id = ?
  DB --> Repository: Profile Basis-Daten
  
  Repository -> DB: SELECT es.*, s.name, sc.name as category\nFROM employee_skills es\nJOIN skills s ON es.skill_id = s.id\nJOIN skill_categories sc ON s.category_id = sc.id\nWHERE es.employee_id = ?
  DB --> Repository: Skills mit Kategorien
  
  Repository -> DB: SELECT pr.*, pos.name as position_name\nFROM projects pr\nLEFT JOIN positions pos ON pr.position_id = pos.id\nWHERE pr.employee_id = ?\nORDER BY pr.start_date DESC
  DB --> Repository: Projekt-Historie
  
  Repository -> DB: SELECT COUNT(*), AVG(proficiency_score)\nFROM employee_skills\nWHERE employee_id = ?
  DB --> Repository: Aggregierte Statistiken
  
  Repository --> Service: UserProfile (vollständig)
  Service --> Controller: UserProfile
  
  == Response Mapping ==
  Controller -> Controller: UserProfileResponseDto.from(profile)
  note right: Mapping Domain -> DTO
  
  Controller --> API: 200 OK (JSON)
  API --> Redux: UserProfile Response
  Redux -> Redux: Cache Result\n(Tag: Profile-{userId})
  Redux --> Browser: Profile Data
end

Browser -> Browser: Rendere Profil-Komponenten
Browser --> Benutzer: Vollständiges Profil anzeigen

@enduml
